From fd82559817a6cebc7e9391f8dc6a25e5e217e131 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rohan8504 <102684130+Rohan8504@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:26:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix: make AI chatbot retrieval and lead scoring accurate

Chatbot
- Match whole words, drop filler words and map everyday phrasing to
  handbook terms ("cost" -> fees, "stay" -> hostel), so the right
  article is returned and off-topic questions no longer match.
- Reply to greetings instead of returning a random article.
- Gemini: configurable model (GEMINI_MODEL, default gemini-2.5-flash),
  API key sent in a header, system instruction plus the last 10
  messages as context, request timeout, and logged errors.
- Pass the most recent 10 messages as history (previously the oldest).
- Fix the fallback link to the events page.

Lead scoring
- Detect Physics + Mathematics properly; arts/commerce streams and
  marks below the 55% minimum are flagged Unqualified for human review.
- Use Class 12 marks as a scoring factor (new leads.class_12_percentage
  column with an automatic migration for existing databases).
- Derive the intake year from the date instead of hardcoding 2026.
- Normalise case/whitespace in inputs; score stored values on create
  and update.

Adds node:test coverage (npm test) and updates README/.env.example.
